  * Read-only scan. Nothing was written, renamed, staged or committed.
  * 600000 band is scanned like every other band. Its 2026-08-10 AUTHORITY
    SUSPENDED ruling concerns design authority, not filename or index format.
  * G04 lists filenames only and applies no date-based grandfathering.
  * G09 compares meaning, not the literal string (000002 s6).
  * G12 is name-level: 000007 stores an indented tree, not full paths.
  * G14 never fires under 990000_legacy_quarantine: those Group C files were
    600000-band artifacts relocated by quarantine, not misused DocumentTypes.
  * Link and existence checks resolve against ALL files on disk, including
    excluded ones, so exclusions never manufacture missing-target findings.
  * G15 reads sql/migrations/*.sql headers and the matching ChangeContract.
    The header is required by 000701 s6.11.1 (2026-08-11), which is not
    retroactive: migrations predating it are tallied as NO_HEADER, never
    counted as violations - 000701 s14.5 forbids editing them.
  * Exit code is always 0. This is a report, not a CI gate.

